```java
// discard the temp. SpimDataFilteringAndGrouping
savedFilteringAndGrouping = null;
```
Reason:
The premature setting of `savedFilteringAndGrouping` to `null` occurs before the asynchronous global optimization process can utilize this data. This results in the necessary filtering and grouping information being discarded, leading to the optimization failing to function correctly.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
// if we discard it right now, but want to do global opt (which runs asynchronously)
// it would not work. therefore, the global optimization will take care of this
savedFilteringAndGrouping = null;
```
Reason:
The fix involves adding a conditional check to ensure that `savedFilteringAndGrouping` is only discarded if global optimization is not going to be executed. This allows the asynchronous global optimization process to access the necessary data, preventing the optimization from failing.

